[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-149955"] :question/problem "What is the value of ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/9e2e705cf17a5dca362c23a23e4d10067ff4390a3f9464dddb6745d78986c02a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is $x\\in [0,1].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-302689/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "60d51ea8-9598-589f-91db-00b4a3099381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302689/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "42791177-a301-5ca8-9f3d-016ee9405d10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302689/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-302689/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302689" :question/id #uuid "1ae9b26e-4b4e-5f6f-aa03-3c0a8cc95e5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-302689" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2))=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/a7e36a5c534a63199ea97985f1301db0c7675adc8fa0d17f33735c61eec9e871.png)\n\nThe domain of   $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty ,$ the graph tends to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-302689/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339380/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "3f26a533-08dc-5210-81c6-a68c05b09c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339380/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c78c4d96-d939-5113-916a-53754e85989c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339380/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "12f5a72f-b190-5748-931c-04aa6c33acba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339380/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer-field/choices ["q-339380/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" "q-339380/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339380" :question/id #uuid "301cfe3d-cf46-5095-bff2-984d0168d45b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339380" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/25cea33f2fc3a3bcdbc10ca03f93bd6059eb7d0a7dfcda5eb59f6f671387aea3.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x+5))=2\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339380/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339380"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339477/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "70a86eac-72b3-53a4-ab40-babc50728e2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339477/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c657a2d2-7ac9-5c68-bb7b-c3788dff7152" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339477/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer-field/choices ["q-339477/field-1/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339477" :question/id #uuid "54e014fa-7fcf-5f0c-af34-9e133e83876b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339477" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/24f07da42a537ded7916fc2440dcf3ee1ccdfc81c7b027b47e97814fec059f5a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\frac{1}{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339477/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339490/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "ff642659-1354-519e-bf4c-124d5941f278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339490/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06e4bd1d-929f-5865-81dd-f24257086327" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339490/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-339490/field-1/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339490" :question/id #uuid "f5e4c600-f08d-56a5-b0e5-8154dc0b42bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-339490" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039967/assets/68f1ebd0457e0c127f8ed6c979feba58196aa6bb43d97d211efa9b39bc33f637.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)) & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339490/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
